    <div class="measure">
      <p>That comparison is the useful habit. An uncertainty budget is a model. Checking it against independent repeat measurements tells you whether the model is honest, or just tidy.</p>

      <h2>What is next</h2>
      <p>The paper's conclusion points to k-corrections, enhancing the uncertainty analysis, and surface metrology. The long-term goal for the laser tracker is surface metrology aligned to the near-field data, so reflector surface defects can be correlated with back-projected aperture fields.</p>
